// "<creature> fights <creature>" [CR#701.14a]: each deals damage equal to its
// power to the other. Each creature is mentioned three times, so it is bound
// where the first damage event first mentions it and read back by identity in
// the rest (`deckmaste_semantics_v2::mentions`): a target is selected once. The
// rule's own wording, "each of those creatures deals damage equal to its power
// to the other creature", is a reciprocal the model lacks; the body writes the
// two damage events instead (routed to
// `semantics-v2-anaphor-resolution-heuristics`). That a creature no longer on
// the battlefield deals no fight damage [CR#701.14b] is the rules' to apply,
// not a guard here: a guard's condition may not introduce its subject. The
// deed's row names no performer.
KeywordAction(
    name: "fight",
    params: [Subject, Subject],
    spelling: "fight",
    grammar: Verb(
        bare: "fight",
        frame_set: Transitive,
    ),
    body: simultaneously([
        dealDamage(Param(0), powerOf(Param(0)), Param(1)),
        dealDamage(Param(1), powerOf(Param(1)), Param(0)),
    ]),
)
